<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guillem II of Pallars Sobirà</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as William II of Pallars Sobirà</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guillem II was the first count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pallars">Pallars</a> Sobirà, a mountain county in the Catalan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyrenees">Pyrenees</a>. When his father Sunyer of Pallars divided his lands in 1011, Guillem received the upper valleys of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/noguera-pallaresa">Noguera Pallaresa</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sort">Sort</a> and Àneu, while his brother Ramon III took Pallars Jussà. His descendants kept the county as the last Catalan county with its own dynasty until the Crown of Aragon took it in the late 15th century.</p></div>
